===Etymology 1===
See [[buy]].

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|buy||ed-form}}.
#: {{ux|en|She '''bought''' an expensive bag last week.}}
#: {{ux|en|People have '''bought''' gas masks.}}
#: {{ux|en|Our products can be '''bought''' at your local store.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=No hiding place
|date=2013-05-25|volume=407|issue=8837|page=74|magazine=w:The Economist
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21578357-plan-assess-peoples-personal-characteristics-their-twitter-streams-no
|passage=In America alone, people spent $170 billion on “direct marketing”—junk mail of both the physical and electronic varieties—last year. Yet of those who received unsolicited adverts through the post, only 3% '''bought''' anything as a result. If the bumf arrived electronically, the take-up rate was 0.1%. And for online adverts the “conversion” into sales was a minuscule 0.01%.}}

====Adjective====
{{head|en|adjective form}}

# (''[[informal]]'', ''[[politics]])'' [[compromised|Compromised]] by [[special interests]]; [[corrupt]].
#: {{ux|en|He's '''bought''' if he votes no on this bill.}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't bother filing a complaint, the regulators are '''bought'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|If union leadership is '''bought''', why should we even pay dues?}}

=====Usage notes=====
It is common to hear native English speakers (particularly in Australia, New Zealand and Britain) use "'''bought'''" when meaning "[[brought]]" (and [[vice versa]]) despite the fact that the two words mean different things [http://wordconstructions.com.au/blog/2008/10/bought-or-brought/][http://www.beedictionary.com/common-errors/bought_vs_brought]. Sometimes this mistake makes its way into print [https://web.archive.org/web/20120304040514/http://thehoopla.com.au/relinquished/], [https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Diaries_Damsels_and_Dastardly_Deeds/NlskEAAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22brought+the+house%7Cproperty%7Cbusiness+from+them%22&pg=PT18&printsec=frontcover], [https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Journal_of_Further_Explorations_in_the_K/fOgtq8NjWusC?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22I%7Cyou%7Che%7Cshe%7Cit%7Cwe%7Cthey+bring%7Cbrings%7Cbrought+it+from+me%7Cyou%7Chim%7Cher%7Cit%7Cus%7Cthem%22&pg=PA122&printsec=frontcover].

