===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰewgʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|bought}}, {{m|enm|bowght}}, {{m|enm|bouȝt}}, {{m|enm|*buȝt}}, probably an alteration of {{m|enm|bight}}, {{m|enm|biȝt}}, {{m|enm|byȝt||bend, bight}} after {{m|enm|bowen}}, {{m|enm|buwen}}, {{m|enm|buȝen||to bow, bend}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|boucht}}, {{m|sco|bucht}}, {{m|sco|bout||bend}}. More at {{m|en|bight}} and {{m|en|bout}}.

